      trivia: "The name 'Room101' derives from the torture chamber in Orwell's Nineteen Eighty-Four — the ultimate room of fear in which each person meets what they dread most. The flagship line 'Namakubi' is Japanese for a severed head, and carries an oni demon logo — a tattoo motif originating in Edo-period ukiyo-e prints, held to symbolise impermanence, respect for one's foe and fearless resolve. That Booth, deployed to Asia as a Marine and later turned jewellery designer, crossed Eastern tattoo imagery with LA street sensibility produced a provocative personality no other brand possesses. Everything began when he met a Camacho employee at a party in 2008 and visited the factory a week later. As Room101 owns no factory, the country of manufacture differs from line to line. That Booth himself dubbed the 13th Anniversary's vivid pink box the 'stinky pinky' is a famous anecdote."
