      trivia: "Baccarat's sweet tip is produced by a special technique of sealing the mouthpiece with a sweet resin known as Indian gum — a vestige of a traditional finish widely seen on Cuban brands in the first half of the twentieth century, leaving a sugar-like sweetness on the tongue. The line name 'The Game' is a playful nod to the casino game of baccarat, while the brand name itself is said to trace back to an old nineteenth-century Cuban marque (originally named Carl Upmann and reportedly made at the Upmann factory). In a modern market that competes on strength, it is a brand of classical aesthetics that deliberately keeps faith with sweetness and lightness."
